  "goodToKnow": "Das Wahlversprechen is an election promise: Wahlversprechen einhalten or brechen. Because Germany is usually governed by coalitions, many promises are traded away in the Koalitionsvertrag (coalition agreement), and parties often say a promise fell victim to coalition talks. Parties set out their promises in a Wahlprogramm. The plural is the same: die Wahlversprechen."
